      "learner_facing": true,
      "markdown": "## A — Sharing the road with riders, pedestrians and large vehicles\nIssuer: Nebraska Department of Motor Vehicles is identified in the private handbook snapshot [A05].\nThe written-test guidance identifies this manual for passenger-car permit and operator applicants [A19].\nSection topic: sharing the road with riders, pedestrians and large vehicles. Passenger-car conduct around motorcycles, bicycles, pedestrians, maintenance equipment, school buses and large vehicles is covered. Motorcycle licensing and commercial-license training are excluded.\nOfficial question count, passing threshold, duration, bank size and weights remain unknown (verify NE-sec14-A-PASS).\nEdition and effective date remain unresolved under the registrar observation-location policy; liveness is verification debt.\nThe learning-loop practice policy does not establish an official exam passing standard.\n",
